erview as well  um  and surprisingly i just i wasn't  expecting it  they offered me a full-time role  and i was only asking for an internship  i think startup startups they have a  different  kind of um time frame of reference than  maybe the bigger companies  and they were like  look you know we need you now like uh  and so  you know i was saying well can i go and  do this  program first and come back in a year  and then start up might not be around in  a year or we might have been doing  something else in a year and so i really  felt like it was a now and ever  opportunity  and um  yeah it was it was very difficult to  think about all of things that i would  have missed out on uh going to insead  the access to like a lifetime  network  um you know just the strengthening of my  my cv  but at the same time i already had this  option here to achieve my objective  which was to transition into the tech  industry move to san francisco move to  the silicon valley right really get all  these impressions exactly exactly and uh  you know obviously there was the 7 000  euro down payment and all of the  expectations i'd set with my friends and  my now wife that this is what i was  going to do for a year um but in the end  i think i just had to be honest with  myself that i was doing the mba for this  particular outcome and here i had a  window of opportunity for this outcome  um and i and i had to take it  and just for the uninitiated i mean  google x is  part of alphabet right so google it's  this incubator where they spin off new  innovative businesses and you had then  the opportunity to join one of them so  indeed you exactly like the outcome that  you wanted to get through the mba  suddenly was presented to you just like  that just by you taking the courage uh  to apply right and  i'm not like why didn't you apply  already before i mean that's the obvious  question right like why did you already  apply a you earlier before you even  started applying to the nba it's it's 